Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

BRepCheck_Shell: the orientation check (Orientation) searched each face at
an edge for the edge with an explorer of all the face's edges, once per
edge of the shell: quadratic in the edges of a face (a shell of 23 430
faces whose two plates hold 23 428 edges each took 9.6 s). For a face of 64
edges or more, the orientations of its edges as its explorer meets them
(the face oriented as in the shell) are now listed once, and the first or
second occurrence of an edge is read from the list; faces of fewer edges,
and an edge a list does not hold, are searched as before. The statuses are
unchanged. The lists are OCCT's own containers: a map per face, shared
through NCollection_Shared, holding each edge's first two orientations
(the only occurrences the check reads) and its count.
Test: geometry/tests/port/p0121-shell-orientation-many-edges.cpp (ctest
geometry.port.0121): the orientation of a plate with 81 holes is right and
a reversed face is still found, as below the threshold; a plate of 19 881
holes is checked within 2 s (the search of each face, quadratic, about 7 s).
